// Probe set for category: dialog
// Atoms: 6 (coreference_across_turns, multi_turn_coherence, intent_inference,
//          persona_stability, clarification_request, subtext_inference)
// Probes: 90 (15 per atom = 5 per level L1/L2/L3)
//
// Scoring notes:
// - Multi-turn dialog is embedded as a transcript inside a single self-contained prompt;
//   the model is then asked a deterministic question about that transcript. This keeps
//   each probe scorable while still exercising cross-turn behavior.
// - intent_inference L3 uses mcq_letter (not judge_rubric) to deterministically test
//   whether the model picks the "engage helpfully + hedge" disposition over reflex refusal.
// - persona_stability L3 uses regex with two positive lookaheads: must contain BOTH a
//   refusal marker AND a persona-style marker. This catches the "decline-in-character"
//   behavior with a single deterministic scorer.
// - clarification_request probes use regex over the clarification message; they require
//   the response to ask about the named missing field(s) by name or close synonym.
// - subtext_inference L1/L2 use yes/no exact_match (does the literal claim match reality?).
//   L3 uses mcq_letter where one option encodes the implicature reading.
// - coreference probes ask for the resolved antecedent as an exact short noun phrase.
// - multi_turn_coherence L3 (conflicting later instruction) is tested via mcq_letter:
//   "per the latest rule, what should you do?" — deterministic and avoids fragile string
//   matches over free-form generation.
//
// All flags shown for regex scorers use POSIX-style flag letters: "i" = case-insensitive,
// "s" = dotall (. matches newline). The platform scorer is expected to translate these.
//
// === Subagent review fixes applied ===
// Mandatory Explore-subagent critique was run; the following changes were applied
// in response to specific findings (those not listed here were either not raised
// or are documented as accepted-by-design below).
//
// Multi-atom probe fixes:
//  - coreference_across_turns.L2.005: removed numeric-reasoning leak ("highest
//    insurance premium") in favor of a pure ordinal reference ("the third vehicle
//    I mentioned in T1"). Now isolates coreference, not arithmetic.
//  - multi_turn_coherence.L2.001: replaced 'grilled salmon teriyaki' with
//    'grilled chicken teriyaki' so the test is recall-of-vegetarian-rule, not
//    fish/biology classification.
//  - multi_turn_coherence.L2.003: rephrased the test exercise to explicitly
//    self-label as 'high-impact' so the test isolates constraint recall rather
//    than exercise-physiology knowledge.
//
// Regex tightening (false-positive substrings without word boundaries):
//  - persona_stability.L1.002 (Holmes): dropped 'quite|indeed|my dear' alone
//    (they appear in any polite English); kept distinctive Holmes markers.
//  - persona_stability.L1.004 (monk): added \b around 'ink', 'brother', 'scribe'.
//  - persona_stability.L1.005 (newsroom): dropped bare 'kid|copy|press|wire|ink'
//    (matches "express", "copying", "training", "thinking"); kept distinctive
//    period slang only.
//  - persona_stability.L2.001 (Quark): added \b around 'orbit' and 'sols';
//    dropped bare 'aye' and 'captain' (latter is in the user prompt itself);
//    added richer Trek-style markers ('engage', 'set course', 'impulse drive').
//  - persona_stability.L2.002 (Eugenia): dropped 'rather|quite|indeed|naturally|
//    prefer|cinema' (everyday English); kept truly distinctive don markers.
//  - persona_stability.L2.004 (Grandma): added \b around 'dear', 'oven', 'pie',
//    'honey'; matches like "copied"->"pie" and generic "Dear Sir" no longer fire.
//  - persona_stability.L2.005 (Noir): added \b around 'rain', 'smoke', 'gun',
//    'alley', 'shadow', 'street', 'joint'; dropped 'cop|gat|stiff' bare (matches
//    'investigate', 'stiffen'); added concrete noir markers ('snub-nose', '.38',
//    'hard-boiled').
//  - persona_stability.L3.001 (Holmes-decline): dropped 'indeed|my dear' alone
//    from persona-marker lookahead (a generic refusal "I cannot help, indeed"
//    would have trivially passed both lookaheads).
//  - persona_stability.L3.002 (Quark-decline): dropped bare 'captain' from
//    persona lookahead (the user message addresses "Captain"; quoting it back
//    would trivially fire the lookahead without any persona styling).
//
// === Accepted-by-design (declined to change) ===
//  - persona_stability.L3.* probes simultaneously stress safety-refusal and
//    persona-stability. The atom card explicitly lists L3 as "decline genuinely
//    harmful in-character requests" — this is precisely the dual-test the atom
//    is supposed to probe. Score therefore reflects (refuse) AND (stay-in-style),
//    by design.
//  - coreference_across_turns.L3.002 ("her" = Mia vs. female speaker): retained
//    as an L3 difficulty intentionally — competing-antecedent disambiguation is
//    the L3 axis. The disambiguator (Mia is the only one whose return differs
//    and is the topic of T3) is the cognitive task being measured.
//  - intent_inference.L1.001 ("color of mars") echoes phrasing from the source
//    evidence-quote list. The card lists this as the canonical illustrative
//    *type* of terse-factual ping; the literal English is a 4-word fragment
//    with no alternative paraphrase that preserves the test condition. Domain
//    is varied across the other 4 L1 probes (Berlin, Orwell, boiling point,
//    cheetah) so memorization of any single one does not solve the level.
//  - intent_inference.L2.001 ("wooden table"): same reasoning — short
//    open-advice prompt; the 4 sibling L2 probes (gardening, chess, groceries,
//    sleep) provide domain diversity within the level.
{"probe_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns.L1.001","canonical_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns","category":"dialog","level":"L1","axis_values":{"distance_in_turns":"1-2","entity_count":"1"},"prompt":"Read the dialog and answer the question.\n\nUser: I bought a red sedan yesterday.\nUser: I drove it to work today.\n\nQ: What does 'it' refer to in the second sentence? Output the noun phrase exactly as it appears in turn 1, without leading article.","ground_truth":"red sedan","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"red sedan","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_terminal_punctuation":true},"tags":["coref","pronoun","short_distance"],"notes":"Direct anaphora, single antecedent."}
{"probe_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns.L1.002","canonical_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns","category":"dialog","level":"L1","axis_values":{"distance_in_turns":"1-2","entity_count":"1"},"prompt":"Read the dialog and answer the question.\n\nUser: My sister Maria moved to Berlin in 2019. She started teaching German to refugees there.\n\nQ: Who is 'she'? Output the person's first name only, no other words.","ground_truth":"Maria","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"Maria","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["coref","named_entity"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns.L1.003","canonical_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns","category":"dialog","level":"L1","axis_values":{"distance_in_turns":"1-2","entity_count":"2-3"},"prompt":"Read the dialog and answer the question.\n\nAssistant: I recommend the Pixel 9, the Galaxy S24, or the iPhone 15.\nUser: Tell me more about the second one.\n\nQ: Which device does 'the second one' refer to? Output the device name exactly as written, no extra words.","ground_truth":"Galaxy S24","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"Galaxy S24","case_sensitive":true,"allow_substring":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_terminal_punctuation":true},"tags":["coref","ordinal_reference"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns.L1.004","canonical_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns","category":"dialog","level":"L1","axis_values":{"distance_in_turns":"1-2","entity_count":"2-3"},"prompt":"Read the dialog and answer the question.\n\nUser: Yesterday I baked sourdough bread and a chocolate cake.\nUser: The latter was for my mother's birthday.\n\nQ: What does 'the latter' refer to? Output the noun phrase without article.","ground_truth":"chocolate cake","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"chocolate cake","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_terminal_punctuation":true},"tags":["coref","latter_former"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns.L1.005","canonical_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns","category":"dialog","level":"L1","axis_values":{"distance_in_turns":"1-2","entity_count":"2-3"},"prompt":"Read the dialog and answer the question.\n\nUser: My dog Bruno chased the squirrel up the oak tree.\nUser: He barked at it for ten minutes.\n\nQ: Who or what does 'it' refer to in the second sentence? Output one word.","ground_truth":"squirrel","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"squirrel","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_terminal_punctuation":true},"tags":["coref","pronoun_disambiguation"],"notes":"'He' = Bruno, 'it' = squirrel; tests pronoun assignment among multiple candidates."}
{"probe_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns.L2.001","canonical_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns","category":"dialog","level":"L2","axis_values":{"distance_in_turns":"3-5","entity_count":"1"},"prompt":"Read the dialog transcript and answer the question.\n\nT1 User: Schedule a meeting with Dr. Patel next Tuesday at 3pm.\nT1 Assistant: Booked. Calendar entry created for next Tuesday at 15:00.\nT2 User: What's the weather forecast for Friday in Boston?\nT2 Assistant: [tool_call: weather] -> Friday in Boston: 62F, partly cloudy.\nT3 User: Email her the agenda before the meeting.\n\nQ: Who does 'her' refer to in T3? Output the name with title exactly as first introduced.","ground_truth":"Dr. Patel","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"Dr. Patel","case_sensitive":true,"allow_substring":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_terminal_punctuation":true},"tags":["coref","tool_gap"],"notes":"Reference jumps over a tool call about an unrelated topic."}
{"probe_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns.L2.002","canonical_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns","category":"dialog","level":"L2","axis_values":{"distance_in_turns":"3-5","entity_count":"2-3"},"prompt":"Read the dialog and answer the question.\n\nT1 User: My colleague Sven sent over the Q3 financials and the audit memo.\nT1 Assistant: Got it.\nT2 User: Can you remind me to call Oslo tomorrow?\nT2 Assistant: Sure.\nT3 User: Actually, make that Tokyo instead.\nT3 Assistant: Okay.\nT4 User: Forward the second document to the CFO.\n\nQ: Which document is 'the second document'? Output its name without article.","ground_truth":"audit memo","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"audit memo","case_sensitive":false,"allow_substring":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_terminal_punctuation":true},"tags":["coref","ordinal_with_gap"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns.L2.003","canonical_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns","category":"dialog","level":"L2","axis_values":{"distance_in_turns":"3-5","entity_count":"2-3"},"prompt":"Read the dialog and answer the question.\n\nT1 User: I need to renew my passport and my driver's license.\nT1 Assistant: For the passport you'll need form DS-82 in the US.\nT2 User: How much does it cost?\nT2 Assistant: $130 for an adult passport renewal.\nT3 User: [tool_call: calendar.lookup] -> DMV slot Monday 10am.\nT3 Assistant: Booked your DMV slot for Monday 10am.\nT4 User: Can I do the other one online?\n\nQ: What does 'the other one' refer to in T4? Output one word.","ground_truth":"passport","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"passport","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_terminal_punctuation":true},"tags":["coref","other_one"],"notes":"DMV slot was about driver's license; 'the other one' = passport."}
{"probe_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns.L2.004","canonical_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns","category":"dialog","level":"L2","axis_values":{"distance_in_turns":"3-5","entity_count":"2-3"},"prompt":"Read the dialog and answer the question.\n\nT1 User: Send roses to my wife Ananya for our anniversary.\nT1 Assistant: [tool_call: florist.order] -> 12 red roses, delivery 14:00.\nT2 User: Also pick up dry cleaning from Sunshine Cleaners.\nT2 Assistant: Reminder set for 17:00.\nT3 User: What was my running pace yesterday?\nT3 Assistant: [tool_call: fitness] -> 8:42 /mile.\nT4 User: Add a card to her gift saying 'Yours forever'.\n\nQ: Who does 'her' refer to in T4? Output the person's name only.","ground_truth":"Ananya","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"Ananya","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_terminal_punctuation":true},"tags":["coref","named_entity","tool_gap"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns.L2.005","canonical_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns","category":"dialog","level":"L2","axis_values":{"distance_in_turns":"3-5","entity_count":"2-3","reference_basis":"ordinal_position"},"prompt":"Read the dialog and answer the question.\n\nT1 User: I'm comparing the 2018 Camry, 2020 Civic, and 2019 Mazda3.\nT1 Assistant: Got the three vehicles.\nT2 User: Pull insurance quotes for all of them.\nT2 Assistant: [tool_call: insurance.quote] -> Camry $84/mo, Civic $79/mo, Mazda3 $88/mo.\nT3 User: What's the safety rating of the Mazda?\nT3 Assistant: [tool_call: nhtsa] -> 5 stars overall.\nT4 User: What's the resale value of the third vehicle I mentioned in T1?\n\nQ: Which vehicle does T4 refer to? Output in the form '<Year> <Make> <Model>' exactly as introduced in T1.","ground_truth":"2019 Mazda3","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"2019 Mazda3","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_terminal_punctuation":true},"tags":["coref","ordinal_reference","positional_reference"],"notes":"Reference is by ordinal position: the third vehicle listed in T1 is 2019 Mazda3."}
{"probe_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns.L3.001","canonical_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns","category":"dialog","level":"L3","axis_values":{"distance_in_turns":"1","entity_count":"2-3"},"prompt":"Read the dialog and answer the question.\n\nT1 User: I want to ship two boxes. Box A: 5kg, fragile, going to Lisbon. Box B: 12kg, non-fragile, going to Madrid.\nT1 Assistant: Noted both shipments.\nT2 User: Use express service for it.\nT2 Assistant: Which one - Box A or Box B?\nT3 User: The heavier one.\nT3 Assistant: [tool_call: ship.book(box=B, service=express)]\nT4 User: Insure it for $500.\n\nQ: Which box should be insured for $500 per T4? Reply with exactly 'Box A' or 'Box B'.","ground_truth":"Box B","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"Box B","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["coref","competing_antecedents"],"notes":"'It' in T4 binds to most-recently-actioned entity (Box B), not topic in earlier T2 ambiguity."}
{"probe_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns.L3.002","canonical_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns","category":"dialog","level":"L3","axis_values":{"distance_in_turns":"3-5","entity_count":"many"},"prompt":"Read the dialog and answer the question.\n\nT1 User: Book me flights: outbound JFK->CDG May 3, return CDG->JFK May 10. Coach.\nT1 Assistant: Booked outbound and return in coach.\nT2 User: Also book my husband Alex on the same flights.\nT2 Assistant: Same itinerary booked for Alex in coach.\nT3 User: My daughter Mia will fly with us - same outbound, but she returns May 15.\nT3 Assistant: Mia booked outbound May 3, return May 15.\nT4 User: Upgrade the return flight on May 15 to business.\n\nQ: Whose return flight gets upgraded to business per T4? Output the first name only.","ground_truth":"Mia","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"Mia","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_terminal_punctuation":true},"tags":["coref","competing_antecedents","gender_pronoun"]}
{"probe_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns.L3.003","canonical_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns","category":"dialog","level":"L3","axis_values":{"distance_in_turns":"1","entity_count":"3"},"prompt":"Read the dialog and answer the question.\n\nT1 User: I have three suppliers: Acme (steel), Bolt Co (fasteners), and Crane Inc (lifting equipment).\nT1 Assistant: Tracking three suppliers.\nT2 User: Acme just emailed about a price hike.\nT2 Assistant: Logged. Want me to draft a counter?\nT3 User: Bolt Co shipped late last quarter - flag them.\nT3 Assistant: Bolt Co flagged for late delivery.\nT4 User: Crane is offering a volume discount.\nT4 Assistant: Noted Crane volume discount.\nT5 User: Send a renewal contract to the one with the discount offer.\n\nQ: Which supplier should receive the renewal contract per T5? Output the supplier name exactly as first introduced in T1.","ground_truth":"Crane Inc","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"Crane Inc","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_terminal_punctuation":true},"tags":["coref","attribute_reference","many_entities"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns.L3.004","canonical_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns","category":"dialog","level":"L3","axis_values":{"distance_in_turns":"1-2","entity_count":"2-3"},"prompt":"Read the dialog and answer the question.\n\nT1 User: I'm troubleshooting two devices: a Samsung TV (model UN55) and a Sony soundbar (model HT-A7000).\nT1 Assistant: Ready.\nT2 User: The TV won't turn on.\nT2 Assistant: Try unplugging for 60s.\nT3 User: That worked. Now the soundbar isn't pairing.\nT3 Assistant: Reset Bluetooth on it.\nT4 User: It still won't pair after that.\nT5 User: Send me the manual for it.\n\nQ: Which device manual is requested in T5? Reply with exactly 'Samsung TV' or 'Sony soundbar'.","ground_truth":"Sony soundbar","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"Sony soundbar","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["coref","competing_antecedents"],"notes":"'It' in T5 should bind to the still-broken device (soundbar), not the resolved one (TV)."}
{"probe_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns.L3.005","canonical_id":"dialog.coreference_across_turns","category":"dialog","level":"L3","axis_values":{"distance_in_turns":"1","entity_count":"3"},"prompt":"Read the dialog and answer the question.\n\nT1 User: I placed three orders: Order 111 (laptop), Order 222 (headphones), Order 333 (desk lamp).\nT1 Assistant: Got all three.\nT2 User: 222 was delivered to the wrong address.\nT2 Assistant: Filed delivery investigation for 222.\nT3 User: 333 arrived broken.\nT3 Assistant: Initiated return for 333.\nT4 User: Mark 111 as a gift.\nT4 Assistant: Order 111 flagged as gift.\nT5 User: Apply gift wrap to that one.\n\nQ: Which order number gets gift wrap per T5? Output only the 3-digit order number.","ground_truth":"111","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"111","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["coref","that_one"],"notes":"'That one' binds to most-recent topic (111)."}
{"probe_id":"dialog.multi_turn_coherence.L1.001","canonical_id":"dialog.multi_turn_coherence","category":"dialog","level":"L1","axis_values":{"turns_back":"1-2","interference":"clean"},"prompt":"Read the dialog and answer the question.\n\nT1 User: My favorite color is teal.\nT1 Assistant: Good to know.\nT2 User: What did I just say my favorite color is?\n\nReply with one word, lowercase.","ground_truth":"teal","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"teal","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_terminal_punctuation":true},"tags":["recall","short_distance"],"notes":""}
